// Title: Delete All Scheduled Tasks
// Sigma ID: 220457c1-1c9f-4c2e-afe6-9598926222c1
// Status: test | Level: high
// Author: Nasreddine Bencherchali (Nextron Systems)
// Date: 2022-09-09 | Modified: -
// ATT&CK: impact, T1489
// Description: Detects the usage of schtasks with the delete flag and the asterisk symbol to delete all tasks
//   from the schedule of the local computer, including tasks scheduled by other users.
// False positives:
//   - Unlikely
// References:
//   - https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/windows-server/administration/windows-commands/schtasks-delete
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/ccbb0369507f796db0b0ae6854c8a2be471b9d84/rules/windows/process_creation/proc_creation_win_schtasks_delete_all.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language 12.4.1, live Defender schema)
// Machine-generated and not tested against real telemetry. Verify before use as a detection.
// Note: 1 wildcard comparison(s) rewritten to 'matches regex' (KQL treats * in contains/endswith/== as a literal character)

DeviceProcessEvents
| where FolderPath endswith "\\schtasks.exe" and (ProcessCommandLine contains " /delete " and ProcessCommandLine matches regex @"(?i)/tn .*" and ProcessCommandLine contains " /f")
